1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:01,874
Three men…

2
00:00:02,194 --> 00:00:04,401
committed the gravest of sins

3
00:00:04,721 --> 00:00:06,852
then… they repented

4
00:00:07,172 --> 00:00:10,295
and the last of them sinned the most

5
00:00:10,615 --> 00:00:11,611
So who are they?

6
00:00:11,931 --> 00:00:12,964
The first…

7
00:00:13,284 --> 00:00:16,799
He was a man… whom travelers feared

8
00:00:17,119 --> 00:00:19,549
He lay in wait for them in the dark of night

9
00:00:19,869 --> 00:00:22,129
and blocked their road

10
00:00:22,449 --> 00:00:24,344
and robbed them of their wealth

11
00:00:24,664 --> 00:00:28,449
until his very name terrified the caravans

12
00:00:28,769 --> 00:00:30,770
Then one night…

13
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:32,730
he climbed a wall

14
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:34,581
seeking to sin

15
00:00:34,901 --> 00:00:38,366
when he heard a voice reciting in the depth of the night

16
00:00:38,686 --> 00:00:44,542
"Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts humble themselves at the remembrance of Allah?" (57:16)

17
00:00:44,862 --> 00:00:47,148
His heart trembled… and he said:

18
00:00:47,468 --> 00:00:50,029
"Yes, my Lord… the time has come."

19
00:00:50,349 --> 00:00:52,935
Then he took shelter in an abandoned ruin

20
00:00:53,255 --> 00:00:55,992
and heard travelers whispering:

21
00:00:56,311 --> 00:01:00,598
"Don't travel tonight… so-and-so is on the road!"

22
00:01:00,918 --> 00:01:03,947
He realized it was him… the one they feared

23
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:05,183
He wept…

24
00:01:05,503 --> 00:01:08,118
and turned to Allah in sincere repentance

25
00:01:08,438 --> 00:01:12,171
Then he left… and lived beside the Sacred House

26
00:01:12,491 --> 00:01:15,637
worshipping, weeping, and teaching people

27
00:01:15,957 --> 00:01:19,171
until he became one of the greatest worshippers and scholars

28
00:01:19,491 --> 00:01:20,475
So who is he?

29
00:01:20,795 --> 00:01:23,700
He is… Al-Fudayl ibn ʿIyad

30
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:26,156
The second man…

31
00:01:26,476 --> 00:01:28,786
He was a slave in Makkah

32
00:01:29,106 --> 00:01:33,076
a spear-thrower… who almost never missed

33
00:01:33,396 --> 00:01:34,974
His master told him:

34
00:01:35,294 --> 00:01:38,548
"Kill so-and-so… and you are free."

35
00:01:38,868 --> 00:01:40,276
On the day of Uhud…

36
00:01:40,596 --> 00:01:42,395
he hid behind a rock

37
00:01:42,715 --> 00:01:45,322
waiting for one man only

38
00:01:45,642 --> 00:01:52,700
a man… the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and one of the dearest people to him

39
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:56,260
He aimed his spear… then threw it

40
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,791
and he fell…

41
00:01:58,111 --> 00:02:03,770
The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) grieved for him deeply

42
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:06,015
He gained his freedom…

43
00:02:06,335 --> 00:02:08,872
but his heart never knew peace

44
00:02:09,192 --> 00:02:12,644
When Makkah was conquered… he fled

45
00:02:12,964 --> 00:02:15,917
and the earth, vast as it is, closed in on him

46
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:20,607
until he was told: "He does not kill anyone who enters his religion."

47
00:02:20,927 --> 00:02:24,211
So he came to Madinah… and embraced Islam

48
00:02:24,531 --> 00:02:29,285
The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him: "Did you kill him?"

49
00:02:29,605 --> 00:02:34,221
Then he said: "Can you keep your face away from me?"

50
00:02:34,541 --> 00:02:37,553
He left… with a vow in his heart

51
00:02:37,873 --> 00:02:43,194
Years later… the Muslims marched against a liar who claimed prophethood

52
00:02:43,514 --> 00:02:45,907
in a garden that came to be called… the Garden of Death

53
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:48,029
He took up the very same spear…

54
00:02:48,349 --> 00:02:50,739
and threw it… striking the liar

55
00:02:51,059 --> 00:02:54,303
and a man of the Ansar struck him with his sword

56
00:02:54,623 --> 00:03:01,006
He said: "I killed the best of people… and I killed the worst of people."

57
00:03:01,326 --> 00:03:03,377
So who is he?

58
00:03:03,697 --> 00:03:07,020
He is… Wahshi ibn Harb

59
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:09,385
And the third man…

60
00:03:09,705 --> 00:03:11,834
his story is the strangest of all

61
00:03:12,154 --> 00:03:15,119
A man from the nations before us…

62
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:18,506
killed ninety-nine people

63
00:03:18,826 --> 00:03:22,475
Then… he felt a heavy weight in his chest

64
00:03:22,795 --> 00:03:26,203
He asked: "Who is the most knowledgeable person on earth?"

65
00:03:26,523 --> 00:03:29,907
They pointed him to a monk in his hermitage

66
00:03:30,227 --> 00:03:36,459
He said: "I have killed ninety-nine people… can I still repent?"

67
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:39,020
The monk said: "No."

68
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:43,420
So he killed him… completing a hundred

69
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:46,915
But a question remained in his heart…

70
00:03:47,235 --> 00:03:50,931
He asked again about the most knowledgeable person on earth

71
00:03:51,251 --> 00:03:53,465
They pointed him to a scholar

72
00:03:53,785 --> 00:03:58,390
He said: "I have killed a hundred people… can I still repent?"

73
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:03,726
The scholar said: "Yes… who can stand between you and repentance?"

74
00:04:04,046 --> 00:04:08,859
"Go to such-and-such land… its people worship Allah

75
00:04:09,178 --> 00:04:12,736
and do not return to your land… for it is a land of evil."

76
00:04:13,056 --> 00:04:14,682
So he set out… and never looked back

77
00:04:15,002 --> 00:04:16,210
He walked day after day

78
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:18,719
until, halfway along the road…

79
00:04:19,039 --> 00:04:20,380
death came to him

80
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:23,010
He pushed himself on his chest toward the righteous land

81
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:27,030
The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him

82
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:32,432
The angels of mercy said: "He came repentant, turning his heart to Allah."

83
00:04:32,752 --> 00:04:36,387
The angels of punishment said: "He never did any good."

84
00:04:36,707 --> 00:04:39,639
It was said: "Measure the distance between the two lands."

85
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:45,251
Allah commanded this land: "Move away"… and that one: "Draw near."

86
00:04:45,571 --> 00:04:49,982
They found him closer to the righteous land… by a single hand-span

87
00:04:50,302 --> 00:04:53,719
So the angels of mercy took his soul… and he was forgiven

88
00:04:54,039 --> 00:04:55,146
So who is he?

89
00:04:55,466 --> 00:04:57,050
Write it in the comments…

90
00:04:57,370 --> 00:05:01,173
And now… what are you waiting for to repent?

91
00:05:01,493 --> 00:05:05,481
Don't delay your repentance… and never despair of Allah's mercy

